WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Welcome to the Accelerometer Learning
Course.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.533
Accelerometers are powerful research tools
because they let us

00:00:07.533 --> 00:00:08.160
move beyond

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.129
self-report and observe patterns of
movement, rest, and sleep

00:00:12.129 --> 00:00:13.040
over time. But

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.792
collecting accelerometer data is only the
beginning. To turn a

00:00:16.792 --> 00:00:17.760
device recording

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.358
into a trustworthy research dataset, every
step has to be

00:00:21.358 --> 00:00:22.620
planned, documented,

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:26.909
and checked. This course gives you a
practical workflow for

00:00:26.909 --> 00:00:28.000
doing that work

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.381
from start to finish. We begin with the
core concepts. What

00:00:32.381 --> 00:00:33.940
does an accelerometer

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:37.096
record? What kinds of outcomes can it
support? Why do device

00:00:37.096 --> 00:00:37.780
placement and

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:42.257
study protocol matter? Then we move into
the hands-on

00:00:42.257 --> 00:00:44.200
workflow. Accelerometry

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.415
turns raw movement into insight about how
people move, rest,

00:00:47.415 --> 00:00:48.540
and sleep. Over eight

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.372
modules, you'll learn the complete
workflow. Module 1

00:00:51.372 --> 00:00:52.120
introduces the

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.711
accelerometer—what it records, and how
placement shapes the

00:00:56.711 --> 00:00:57.800
data. Module 2

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:01.304
covers programming and downloading the
device. Module 3,

00:01:01.304 --> 00:01:02.180
organizing and

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:06.550
converting your files. Module 4 sets up R
and GGIR to process

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:07.840
the data. Module 5

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.816
checks data quality. Module 6 cleans and
standardizes the

00:01:11.816 --> 00:01:13.420
output. Module 7 builds

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:17.050
the final dataset in Stata. And Module 8
is a knowledge check

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:18.180
to consolidate what

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:22.475
you've learned. After that, we show how
raw device files can

00:01:22.475 --> 00:01:23.620
be converted and

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:28.629
processed. The course uses ActiLife, R,
GGIR, and Stata as the

00:01:28.629 --> 00:01:29.760
main examples.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:33.483
These tools help move the data from raw
acceleration signals

00:01:33.483 --> 00:01:34.600
into interpretable

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:38.795
summaries of physical activity, sedentary
behavior, and

00:01:38.795 --> 00:01:40.320
sleep-wake patterns.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:44.167
Just as important, you will learn how to
inspect data quality.

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:45.160
A single summary

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:48.277
number can hide problems, so the course
emphasizes visual

00:01:48.277 --> 00:01:49.480
checks, clear decision

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:54.034
rules, and careful notes about exclusions
or concerns. By the

00:01:54.034 --> 00:01:54.780
end of the

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.385
course, you should understand the complete
path from planning

00:01:57.385 --> 00:01:57.940
and deploying

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:01.592
an accelerometer to preparing an
analysis-ready dataset. You

00:02:01.592 --> 00:02:02.140
will also

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:05.169
know where protocol decisions must be
adapted for the

00:02:05.169 --> 00:02:06.540
population, device, wear

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:11.242
location, and research question in your
own study. This course

00:02:11.242 --> 00:02:12.380
is designed for

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:15.740
students, research assistants, and lab
members who want a

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:16.860
clear, reproducible

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.841
introduction to accelerometer-based
measurement. Start with

00:02:19.841 --> 00:02:20.700
the first module,

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.205
accelerometer introduction, and then
follow the workflow

00:02:24.205 --> 00:02:25.520
step-by-step. Welcome

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.960
to the course.
